---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { repository, url } from '../lib/site';
import courtyard from '../assets/courtyard.png';
import cluster from '../assets/cluster.png';
import canopy from '../assets/canopy.png';
const places = [
  { image: courtyard, number: '01', title: 'A courtyard, together.', text: 'Shared walls. A common garden. Find the balance between personal space and shared systems.' },
  { image: cluster, number: '02', title: 'A little more room.', text: 'Spread out into a detached village. See what changes when every home has its own envelope.' },
  { image: canopy, number: '03', title: 'A different perspective.', text: 'Try elevated cabins. Experiment with lighter materials and the limits of declared supports.' },
];
---
<Base>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="wrap relative grid items-center gap-4 overflow-hidden pb-12 pt-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:pb-20 lg:pt-18">
      <div class="relative z-10 pb-4 lg:pb-10">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-7 flex items-center gap-2.5"><span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-forest"></span> A community simulation, open to everyone</p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(3.5rem,6.4vw,6.3rem)] leading-[1.04] font-medium tracking-[-0.055em]">Small places.<br /><span class="text-forest">Big possibilities.</span></h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-md text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">What makes a place good to live in? Build a small community, try an idea, and see how life changes for the people who call it home.</p>
        <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="button button-primary" href={url('play/')}>Play in your browser <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href={url('docs/getting-started/')}>Start exploring <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
        <p class="mt-5 text-xs text-muted">Free to play. Open source. Yours to experiment with.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="relative -mx-6 sm:-mx-10 lg:-mr-24 lg:-ml-10">
        <div class="absolute top-[15%] left-[13%] h-[70%] w-[73%] rounded-full bg-leaf/55 blur-3xl"></div>
        <Image src={courtyard} alt="An in-game courtyard of eight small homes surrounding a shared garden, with solar panels and common utilities." width={1120} height={840} loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" class="relative w-full mix-blend-multiply" />
        <figcaption class="absolute right-[12%] bottom-[10%] flex items-center gap-3 rounded-xl border border-line bg-paper/95 px-4 py-3 shadow-sm"><span class="grid size-8 place-items-center rounded-full bg-leaf text-forest" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><div><span class="block text-xs font-semibold">One place. Many possible futures.</span><span class="text-[11px] text-muted">The community lab · playable prototype</span></div></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <div class="border-y border-line bg-white/35"><div class="wrap flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-3 py-5 text-xs text-muted"><span>BUILT FOR CURIOSITY</span><span>24 neighbours</span><span>One year of possibilities</span><span>Materials you can remix</span><span class="font-semibold text-forest">MIT licensed ↗</span></div></div>
    <section class="wrap py-20 lg:py-28">
      <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 md:items-end"><div><p class="eyebrow mb-4">A small world with real tradeoffs</p><h2 class="font-display text-4xl leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">There’s more than one<br />way to live well.</h2></div><p class="max-w-lg text-base leading-relaxed text-muted md:justify-self-end">Warm homes need energy. Shared services need care. Lower bills can mean higher upfront costs. Start with a place you understand, then test what could make it better.</p></div>
      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        {places.map((place) => <article><div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-line bg-[#eeeedf]"><span class="absolute top-4 left-4 z-10 font-mono text-xs text-muted">{place.number} / SETTLEMENT STUDY</span><Image src={place.image} alt={`${place.title} A scene rendered by the Courtyard Block game.`} width={560} height={420} loading="lazy" class="w-full mix-blend-multiply transition-transform duration-500 hover:scale-[1.035]" /></div><h3 class="mt-6 font-display text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight">{place.title}</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{place.text}</p></article>)}
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="bg-ink py-20 text-paper"><div class="wrap grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr] lg:gap-24"><div><p class="eyebrow mb-5 text-leaf/70!">A loop for curious minds</p><h2 class="font-display text-4xl leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Try something.<br />Learn something.<br /><span class="text-[#b7d69c]">Try something else.</span></h2><p class="mt-6 max-w-sm text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper/65">No perfect score to chase. Notice a problem, make a change, and discover the next question.</p></div><div class="grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2">{[
        ['01', 'Make a change', 'Pick a layout. Insulate a home. Add rainwater storage. Give your experiment a question.'],
        ['02', 'Watch a year', 'Run a winter or a full year. Both designs meet the same weather and the same households.'],
        ['03', 'Follow the people', 'Look beyond averages. Find out who is cold, who can pay their bills, and where services struggle.'],
        ['04', 'Share a possibility', 'Keep your inputs and assumptions together. Send a complete experiment to a friend to remix.'],
      ].map(([number, title, text]) => <article><span class="font-mono text-xs text-[#b7d69c]">{number}</span><h3 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold">{title}</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper/65">{text}</p></article>)}</div></div></section>
    <section class="wrap grid gap-12 py-20 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center lg:gap-24 lg:py-28">
      <div><p class="eyebrow mb-5">The best idea might be yours</p><h2 class="font-display text-4xl leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Make a world<br />worth sharing.</h2><p class="mt-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">Start with the built-in workshop. Change a material, assemble a wall, add evidence, and try it in your community. Go further with editable data packs and your own weather records.</p><div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="button button-primary" href={url('docs/data-reference/')}>Make your first mod <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href={repository}>Explore the source ↗</a></div></div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white/70 p-7 sm:p-10"><div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-line pb-5"><span class="eyebrow">A material is a starting point</span><span class="pill bg-leaf/50">Editable</span></div><div class="py-6"><span class="text-xs text-muted">YOUR NEXT EXPERIMENT</span><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl">A warmer kind of wall.</h3></div><dl class="space-y-0 text-sm">{[['Material layers', 'Timber + insulation'], ['Thermal properties', 'Defined by your data'], ['Costs & assumptions', 'Visible and inspectable'], ['Your evidence', 'Sources travel with the mod']].map(([label, value]) => <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between gap-2 border-t border-line py-4"><dt class="text-muted">{label}</dt><dd class="font-medium">{value}</dd></div>)}</dl><p class="mt-5 rounded-lg bg-paper p-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted">The same model runs every supported assembly. AI can help draft a pack; you decide which assumptions to test.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="wrap"><div class="flex flex-col justify-between gap-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-leaf/30 p-8 md:flex-row md:items-center md:p-12"><div><p class="eyebrow mb-3">A foundation we can build on</p><h2 class="font-display text-3xl tracking-tight">Open code. Open questions.</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">This is an early, bounded simulation. Today: heat, utilities, costs and one year of fixed households. The inputs are illustrative. More construction methods, richer community life and longer horizons are questions for the road ahead.</p></div><a class="button button-secondary shrink-0 bg-paper" href={url('docs/moddability/')}>Read the direction →</a></div></section>
  </main>
</Base>
